1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind, and a sound body.

2
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
A bomb, huh?

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Over there! Look it!

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Huh?

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
I've arranged at random, without any symmetry. Absolutely disgusting.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,000
I heard an explosion.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
It must be one of the tadpole bombs I set. We need to hurry!

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
I smell something.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Yes. We're almost there now. The Kishin is just ahead.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:04,000
You fools, I'm the one who's leading. Things are going to get interesting now.

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Hey, man!

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:31,400
繋いだ魂の火が胸を刺すなら 言葉よりもっと強い響きが今聞こえるか

13
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:49,140
Six人目も合わさず運命まで絡んでく

14
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:54,840
行き先もらったポテル食えない夜の端で

15
00:01:54,840 --> 00:02:04,240
不可愛しすぎた眩しさが悪い夢に続いても

16
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:11,560
繋いだ魂の火が胸を刺すなら

17
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:18,320
言葉よりもっと強い響きが今聞こえるか

18
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:23,200
出会った理由は途絶びに突きつけられて

19
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:29,200
触れた瞬間の傷の分だけ確かになれる

20
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:38,720
It's an abomination

21
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:44,040
Such an inconsistent arrangement is unconscionable

22
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:45,200
Damn it

23
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:48,340
Hey kid, let's forget about consistency for now

24
00:02:48,340 --> 00:02:50,060
We can pass right on through

25
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:52,060
Just don't look at them for too long

26
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:57,540
It's starting to make me sick

27
00:02:57,540 --> 00:02:58,640
That would feel good

28
00:02:58,640 --> 00:02:59,320
See?

29
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:00,440
What did I tell you?

30
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:01,500
Okay

31
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:05,700
In your defense, I suppose poorly arranged bombs are as terrifying to you

32
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:08,100
as a path full of monsters would be to most normal people

33
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:12,780
You know, it might not just be the whole inconsistent arrangement thingy

34
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:14,260
Those are bombs after all

35
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:15,560
Who wouldn't be scared?

36
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:18,460
Yeah, it's possible you got a point there

37
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:20,500
This trap may be the end of me

38
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:22,520
It's over

39
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:24,320
Whoa, hold on just a sec

40
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:27,300
Vacation's gonna wake back up if you give up this easily

41
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:28,500
You're a reaper

42
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,680
If you can't do this, then who can?

43
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:32,260
You can say whatever you want

44
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:34,380
I'm nothing but filthy reaper scum

45
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:36,740
Just put me by the curb on garbage day

46
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:40,960
It's your turn, Patty

47
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:43,220
Tell him in that special way that you have

48
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:43,820
Okay

49
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:49,320
Get your ass moving now, damn you

50
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:56,880
Nice

51
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:59,340
He's using the blast to give himself more momentum

52
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:03,180
Well done

53
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:06,400
You did an incredible job of finally getting his butt moving, Patty

54
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,340
Amazing

55
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:09,540
Yeah, it was really scary, wasn't I, sis?

56
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:11,900
Dammit, Patty, I hate you so much

57
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:13,880
I really, really hate you

58
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:19,160
Hang in there

59
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:21,040
It's just going to be a little bit longer

60
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:23,560
Something's following us at breakneck speed

61
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:24,620
And it's catching up

62
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:27,460
Free, we've got to inject the black blood into the Kishin

63
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:29,680
If anything happens to this case before we do

64
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:31,700
Then Medusa's going to slaughter us both

65
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:33,720
I know she will, but I've got an idea

66
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:35,960
Let me borrow that tadpole you're riding on

67
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:37,020
I'm gonna need it

68
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:37,940
Huh?

69
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,100
Tadpole Jackson?

70
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,400
What are you gonna do with him?

71
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:42,680
Not much

72
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:44,580
Just get a jump on the enemy

73
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:49,620
May my soul reach you

74
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:52,400
A dry heart inside unbearable isolation

75
00:04:52,400 --> 00:05:00,280
Let's go

76
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:04,320
It's all just so funny, you know?

77
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:05,840
Quit it

78
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:06,920
Please stop

79
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,300
You're all wobbly and giggly

80
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:09,240
I don't like it

81
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,620
Stay away from me

82
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:13,060
I told you

83
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:15,560
I hate wobbly giggle

84
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:18,740
That's too bad

85
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:19,520
I don't like him

86
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:25,300
Hey, it's black

87
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:26,120
It's so pretty

88
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:27,720
What's with this?

89
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,520
She's really lost it now

90
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:31,400
Go on, hurt me some more

91
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:33,120
You can do better than this, can't you?

92
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:48,660
So this is madness

93
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:51,840
It protects your partner from feeling any fear

94
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:54,500
Her soul and her opponent's soul are irrelevant

95
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:56,440
They have nothing to do with this fight

96
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,540
Come on, give me something new

97
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:02,200
Can't you do anything like eye gouging or fish hooking?

98
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,120
No?

99
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,060
Well, maybe you'd like to tear off my tongue

100
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:09,920
What are you doing out there, Maka?

101
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:12,980
Getting your tongue torn off was not part of the plan, remember?

102
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:19,200
Damn it

103
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:21,440
Now I'm getting pulled into the madness, too

104
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,880
Hurry, Maka

105
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:24,920
Or you won't ever be able to come back

106
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:27,180
Soul

107
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:31,640
Oh, wow

108
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:33,340
That's embarrassing

109
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:36,060
It's not that different from how you normally are

110
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:38,880
Now hurry up and do whatever you need to do

111
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:41,140
Yeah, I'm working on it

112
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:43,220
I think I can do this

113
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:46,740
I had a weird kind of premonition when I was sane

114
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:50,660
Now that I've got the same madness as Corona

115
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:54,540
I can match our soul wavelengths and find out what it is

116
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:56,880
Feel it

117
00:06:56,880 --> 00:07:04,700
Look at this

118
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:08,520
This is my soul

119
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:10,680
It really is pretty tiny

120
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:16,340
Another one

121
00:07:16,340 --> 00:07:20,760
It's not in the best shape

122
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:23,160
A little twisted, a bit worse for the wear

123
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:25,320
Kind of rough around the edges, too

124
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,720
But it's always there for me

125
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:29,720
This is my soul eater soul

126
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:35,880
Now where's Krona's soul?

127
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:44,700
That must be his soul up there

128
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:53,280
It's hard to explain

129
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:56,420
But I'm sensing a very dry wavelength

130
00:07:56,420 --> 00:08:06,840
A desert?

131
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:09,540
It almost looks like it could be a beach

132
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:12,220
But with no ocean

133
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:19,140
Krona?

134
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:25,400
I'm gonna make you pay for this

135
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,980
He was my food slave

136
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:31,640
Um pumpkin pumpkin

137
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:33,640
Pumpkin pumpkin

138
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:34,640
Pumpkin pumpkin

139
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:42,580
Would you like some more?

140
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:47,520
It's important for a lady to be limber and flexible

141
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:48,960
Five against one

142
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:51,000
And there's not a scratch on my perfect body

143
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,880
They could use some practice

144
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:57,620
The newly stabbed up

145
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:07,720
And there's a slap

146
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:08,320
Chichi

147
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:10,120
Chee

148
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:10,700
Chee

149
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,560
Chee

150
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:12,740
Chee

151
00:09:12,740 --> 00:09:14,540
Chee

152
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:15,740
Chee

153
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:16,680
Chee

154
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:17,640
Chee

155
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:17,900
Chee

156
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:18,620
Chee

157
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:20,040
Chee

158
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:20,420
Chee

159
00:09:20,420 --> 00:09:20,700
Chee

160
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:21,180
Chee

161
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:21,540
Chee

162
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:21,640
Chee

163
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:21,920
Chee

164
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:22,020
Chee

165
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:25,480
I wouldn't get too cocky if I were you, little kitty.

166
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:28,200
Don't you know that the cornered rat will bite the cat?

167
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:31,440
Hot, hot, hot, hot!

168
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:38,240
Do you think I'm going to let you get away with trying to seduce men on my turn?

169
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:41,080
Oh, oh, oh, no.

170
00:09:41,460 --> 00:09:42,780
I can't take anymore.

171
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:51,260
You're going to be one dead feline.

172
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:53,920
Big talk coming from a quintuple-decker mousy.

173
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:58,600
Huh, what a distasteful outfit.

174
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:00,500
Like you're really one to talk.

175
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:03,060
Isn't this top a little drafty?

176
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:06,560
Didn't you die or something?

177
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:14,220
At long last, the Black Blood is ready.

178
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:18,880
All that remains now is to inject it into the Kishin and revive it.

179
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:22,240
You can keep struggling as long as you want, but it's no use.

180
00:10:22,780 --> 00:10:25,080
My plan is going to succeed no matter what.

181
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:26,000
Tell me.

182
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:30,860
If you do get your way and the Kishin is revived, what will happen to the Demon Sword child?

183
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:34,460
Your Black Blood research is complete.

184
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:37,380
You're done with the experiment for which you needed this child.

185
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:38,360
So now?

186
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,220
Oh, please.

187
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,980
What am I going to do with it?

188
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,180
Let's see.

189
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:46,340
I ordered it around all its life, so now it's lacking in independence.

190
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:49,160
One reason not to be an overbearing mother, I suppose.

191
00:10:49,740 --> 00:10:51,420
Anyway, Corona didn't turn out well.

192
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:52,780
It was a failure of mine.

193
00:10:52,780 --> 00:10:55,440
Lacking independence or not, he's your kid.

194
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:57,000
What are you going to do with him?

195
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:59,360
What will you do with your child?

196
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:02,220
Quit laughing.

197
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:04,300
What's got you two so irritated?

198
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:05,500
You sound ridiculous.

199
00:11:06,460 --> 00:11:09,100
Do I really have to tell you what you already know?

200
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:10,520
Think about it this way.

201
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:12,820
Why would I keep something that I no longer need?

202
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:14,980
It makes much more sense to throw it away.

203
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:16,580
But why do you ask?

204
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:17,760
Do you want it?

205
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:20,800
You can have my hand-me-downs if you like.

206
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:23,440
You could use it for your experiments or something.

207
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:25,220
You evil witch.

208
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:28,160
You damn witch.

209
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:29,820
Yes, what is it?

210
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:31,960
You.

211
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:33,840
Why you.

212
00:11:34,380 --> 00:11:35,180
That all?

213
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:39,600
If you're going to talk about something, the least you can do is know what you're going to say.

214
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:42,540
Spirit, watch it.

215
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:43,860
You shouldn't be so reckless.

216
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:48,080
Oh, great.

217
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,720
Don't snivel like a little baby.

218
00:11:51,140 --> 00:11:52,400
You're a grown man.

219
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:53,900
I know that, damn it.

220
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:56,460
But unlike you, Stein, I am a parent.

221
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,220
So to me, this is...

222
00:11:58,220 --> 00:11:59,660
How do I explain it to you?

223
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:01,540
It's unforgivable.

224
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:07,220
If a child's own mother abandons him, who else in the world will he be able to turn to?

225
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:08,200
Yes, exactly.

226
00:12:08,340 --> 00:12:10,300
That's what I've been trying to say all along.

227
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:15,280
In any case, we're definitely going to defeat her.

228
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:17,740
That's pretty much been the plan this whole time.

229
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:23,440
What should I do now that I'm here?

230
00:12:26,740 --> 00:12:27,620
Right here.

231
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:29,920
This is my area.

232
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:32,360
I'm drawing the line to mark it.

233
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:39,800
But what should I do now?

234
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:46,340
Kicking up sand doesn't seem to do me any good.

235
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:49,580
And there's not much else besides sand in this place.

236
00:12:49,580 --> 00:12:53,040
Even the sun is lifeless.

237
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:55,680
It's just hanging there asleep in the sky.

238
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:00,720
Doing nothing is probably the best plan.

239
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:12,780
Hey.

240
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:18,080
My name is Krona.

241
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:20,040
Of course.

242
00:13:20,540 --> 00:13:22,600
It always shows up when I'm doing nothing.

243
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:25,200
Can I ask you some questions?

244
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:28,400
Here goes.

245
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:31,980
And here we go with the questions again.

246
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:34,420
When all I really want to do is nothing.

247
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:37,260
Can I pass if I want?

248
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:38,740
That's up to you, I guess.

249
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:40,540
Here are my questions.

250
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:42,520
First question.

251
00:13:43,060 --> 00:13:43,760
What's your name?

252
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:45,520
I pass.

253
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:47,160
That was an easy one.

254
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:49,400
You mean you won't even say what your name is?

255
00:13:49,940 --> 00:13:51,120
Why do you think that is?

256
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:53,140
I pass.

257
00:13:53,780 --> 00:13:56,040
Here, let me see if I can answer that one for you.

258
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:58,700
Basically, you can't answer other people's questions.

259
00:13:59,020 --> 00:14:01,720
So you question yourself in order to keep your mind intact.

260
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:02,780
Sound about right?

261
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:04,840
Pass.

262
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:06,180
Another pass?

263
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,800
You need to start answering.

264
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:10,500
This isn't even self-questioning at this point.

265
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:11,540
Wouldn't you agree?

266
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:12,500
Pass.

267
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:16,960
Are you hoping someone will start paying attention to you if you act troubled enough?

268
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:20,020
But don't you realize you're alone?

269
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:23,000
That no one actually cares about your suffering?

270
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:24,440
I pass.

271
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:27,200
That makes five passes.

272
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:30,360
Let's change the subject, then.

273
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:32,100
We can talk about the little one.

274
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:34,640
When you beat it up, that was your first time.

275
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,780
How did you feel after you defeated it?

